A directive written above alpha binds alpha only, though a second line
directive renders bravo on alpha's line: bravo is reported.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//line main.go:19:1
//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- keep alpha
func alpha() {}

//line main.go:20:1
func bravo() {}
